    <footnotes>
        <footnote id="F1">As described in the issuer's registration statement on Form S-1 (File No. 333-267399) under the heading &quot;Description of Securities,&quot; the shares of Class B common stock of the issuer will automatically convert into shares of Class A common stock of the issuer at the time of the issuer's initial business combination, on a one-for-one basis, subject to certain adjustments described therein, and have no expiration date.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F2">On November 16, 2026, Alvin Wang LLC, an entity controlled by the Reporting Person, resigned as the managing member of ALWA Sponsor LLC (the &quot;Sponsor&quot;). As a result of such resignation, the Reporting Person is no longer deemed to have beneficial ownership, directly or indirectly, of the reported securities held by the Sponsor.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F3">Alvin Wang LLC transferred its membership interest in the Sponsor pursuant to certain purchase agreement dated November 16, 2026, representing approximately 81.39% of the Sponsor's total membership interests, to Remcan Holdings LLC. The aggregate consideration for the transfer is USD 2,000,000, payable in two installments: USD 1,000,000 becomes due upon the closing of the issuer's business combination, and USD 1,000,000 becomes due within ninety days thereafter. In connection with the transfer, Alvin Wang LLC resigned as the managing member of the Sponsor.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F4">The Reporting Person controls Alvin Wang LLC, which was the managing member of the Sponsor and, as such, the Reporting Person may have been deemed to have beneficial ownership of the reported securities held by the Sponsor. On November 16, 2026, Alvin Wang LLC resigned as the managing member of the Sponsor. As a result of such resignation, the Reporting Person is no longer deemed to have beneficial ownership, directly or indirectly, of the reported securities.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F5">The warrants become exercisable on the later of (i) 30 days after the completion of the issuer's initial business combination and (ii) 12 months from the date of the issuer's final prospectus filed in connection with the issuer's initial public offer dated March 22, 2023 (File No. 333-267399).</footnote>
        <footnote id="F6">The warrants expire 5 years after the completion of the issuer's initial business combination or earlier upon redemption or liquidation, as described in the registrant's prospectus filed with the SEC.</footnote>
